 Portfolio Statement

Portfolio consists record of works from last couple of years, it is an attempt of organise them in specific order and kind of narration, which explains in best possible way my approach to design and art.  E-folio doesn’t contain examples of pieces or sketches that I was writing about in my personal statement – I tried to describe my motivation and dreams there instead.
First two slides include jewellery works. Made with traditional techniques in silver and brass, covered with enamel or with stones set in.  Some of them use engravings, e.g. in necklace with ginkgo leafes which were made in order to underline resemblance to natural form. Slide with the title „tanguy’s forms” pictures work which was part of my diploma in the end of high school and it was inspired by works of surrealist. Organic forms and hollow inside;  focused on turning into literal translation from the paintings; flat surface to three dimensional living creature. 
My way of searching in the field of jewellery has also its similarity in photography – it is very often the main and base for future discoveries. In this process freedom of expression is very important to me, even if it might be looking like chaos (sketches). I like exaggerations; looking for shapes in abstract like compositions, developing until it ends without any sign of meaning.
Sixth slide is about sculpture, it is made with bogwood and was part of the work for the archeological museum in Poznan city. The same wood was excavated from archeological site on grounds of the first polish settlements. Its shape is associated with the symbol of Poznan - star. Hanging from the ceiling clock like construction was sensitive to the smallest vibrations in the air, which reflected the presence of the observer and made whole thing interactive. Above construction black circle of clock-face was painted with ointment made of pigment from the very same bogwood.  
The rest of the set consists examples of works from different fields of my interest. You can find there „digital experiments” which captures the process of finding the right form and where I used Mathlab software to process image into graphic ; „pelcery” - etching prints where my home town neighborhood is depicted and many paintings created in many different techniques.


